% fork_1_circular_deref.glp - FORK-1 (C-19 / GAP-G5 C-15): the circular-term
% deref/display discriminator. This was an OPEN owner-gated fork (Option A loud-all
% vs Option B structural-vs-cycle); RESOLVED owner-directed on 2026-07-13 in favour
% of Option B — STRUCTURAL CYCLE DETECTION.
%
% A self-referential term is formed by the REPL goal `X = f(X?)` (SRSW-valid: one
% writer on the left, one reader inside `f`; the runtime deref then loops on the
% shared cell). All three instances now CONVERGE: Dart, C#, and the Gleam instance
% detect the cycle and render `<circular>` at the revisit (e.g. `f(f(<circular>))`,
% `pair(a, pair(a, <circular>))`) — no loop, no silent cut. This file names the case
% (now an AGREEING corpus block) and holds a loadable non-circular baseline (`wrap`).

SelfRef ::= f(SelfRef) ; base.

exported procedure wrap(SelfRef?, SelfRef).
wrap(X, f(X?)).
